Hm, yeah, actually, why even bother involving `p_max_collisions` at all in that case. `result.size() / 2` should pretty much always be equal to `p_max_collisions`, but might be smaller because of `resize` potentially failing, so all we really want to do is this:

```cpp
void PhysicsCollideShapeResult3D::set_max_collisions(int p_max_collisions) {
	ERR_FAIL_COND(p_max_collisions < 0);
	result.resize(2 * p_max_collisions);
	collision_count = MIN(collision_count, result.size() / 2);
}
```

That seems fairly obvious in hindsight I guess.
